---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Page
	title="About Us & Editorial Policy"
	description={'Who we are, what we cover and the editorial standards behind ' + SITE_TITLE + '.'}
>
	<p>
		{SITE_TITLE} covers four areas: sports, TV and streaming, celebrity news, and crime and
		justice. Our goal is simple: explain what happened, why it matters and where the information
		comes from, in plain language.
	</p>

	<h2>Editorial standards</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Sources first.</strong> Every news article links to its original sources, such as
			official statements, court records, league announcements or reporting by established
			outlets.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Original writing.</strong> We write our own summaries and analysis. We do not copy
			articles from other publications.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Celebrity news from official sources.</strong> We report what public figures and
			their representatives confirm. We do not publish unverified rumors about private lives,
			health or relationships.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Fair crime coverage.</strong> People charged with a crime are presumed innocent
			until proven guilty, and we describe accusations as alleged. We avoid graphic details and
			do not identify minors or victims of sexual crimes.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Images.</strong> We only use images we have the right to use, and we credit them.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Corrections</h2>
	<p>
		If we get something wrong, we fix it and add an update date to the article. To report an
		error, email <a href={'mailto:' + CONTACT_EMAIL}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the article link and
		what needs correcting.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		News tips, corrections and other questions are welcome on our
		<a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
	</p>
</Page>
